const faq = [
  { q: 'Where does the Fan-tailed Raven nest?', a: 'The Fan-tailed Raven is a cliff-nester throughout its range — the Horn of Africa, Red Sea coast, Arabian Peninsula, and parts of the Middle East. It places its nest on a ledge, in a crevice, or in a cave entrance on a steep cliff face. Its strong association with cliffs and gorges defines its entire ecology, from foraging to roosting to nesting.' },
  { q: 'When does the Fan-tailed Raven breed?', a: 'Breeding season varies across the Fan-tailed Raven\'s wide range. In the Horn of Africa (Ethiopia, Somalia, Eritrea), breeding is documented from approximately November to April, coinciding with the drier periods. In the Arabian Peninsula, breeding occurs roughly January to April. The timing reflects local climatic patterns rather than a uniform continental calendar.' },
